    "lawCode": "Amd §247, Mil L",
    "lawSection": "Military Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5372\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the military law, in relation to the issuance of a New\nYork State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo establish the Afghanistan Iraq War Commemorative Medal for members of\nthe armed forces or organized militia serving abroad in the Afghanistan\nWar during the period of time from October 7, 2001 through August 30,\n2021.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 247 of the Military Law by adding a new subdi-\nvision which authorizes the Adjutant General to present in the name of\nthe legislature of the State of New York, a medal to be known as the\n\"New York State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal.\"\n\nSection 2 amends Subdivision 4 of Section 247 of the Military Law to\ninclude the New York State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal in this\nsection, with the other state medals, that do not require recipients to\nhave been a resident of the State of New York at the time of his or her\nentry into the armed forces or organized militia.\n\nSection 3 states the effective date. It also authorizes the Division of\nMilitary and Naval Affairs to promulgate any and all rules and regu-\nlations and take any other measures necessary to implement the\nprovisions of this act.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew Yorkers pride themselves on recognizing and honoring the courageous\nservice and sacrifice of the heroic members of our armed forces- includ-\ning our most recent conflicts. Thousands of New Yorkers served hero-\nically during the 2001-2021 Afghanistan War. Many also made the ultimate\nsacrifice. It is only appropriate that the State acknowledge and honor\nthe service of those who fought in Afghanistan.  The creation of this\ncommemorative medal will provide a small token of thanks and appreci-\nation for those that. served.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: S8475/A9443 - Passed Senate/Died in Veterans Affairs\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect 120 days after it shall have become law.\n",
