    "lawCode": "Amd §247, Mil L",
    "lawSection": "Military Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5372A\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the military law, in relation to the issuance of a New\nYork State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo establish the Afghanistan Iraq War Commemorative Medal for members of\nthe armed forces serving in Afghanistan War during the period of time\nfrom October 7, 2001 through August 30, 2021.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 247 of the Military Law by adding a new subdi-\nvision 1-f which authorizes the Adjutant General to present in the name\nof the legislature of the State of New York, a medal to be known as the\n\"New York State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal.\"\n\nSection 2 amends Subdivision 4 of Section 247 of the Military Law, to\ninclude the New York State Afghanistan War Commemorative Medal in this\nsection, with the other state medals, that do not require the recipient\nof such medals to have been a resident of the State of New York at the\ntime of his or her entry into the armed forces or organized militia.\n\nSection 3 states the effective date to be on the first day of January\nafter this act shall become law. It also authorizes the Division of\nMilitary and Naval Affairs to promulgate any and all rules and regu-\nlations and take any other measures necessary to implement the\nprovisions of this act.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew Yorkers pride themselves on recognizing and honoring the courageous\nservice and sacrifice of the heroic members of our armed forces. This\nincludes are-most recent conflicts. Thousands of New Yorkers served\nheroically during the 2001-2021 Afghanistan War. Many also made the\nultimate sacrifice. It is only appropriate that the State acknowledge\nand honor the service of those who fought in Afghanistan. The creation\nof this commemorative medal will provide a small token of thanks and\nappreciation for those that served.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S8475/A.9443-Passed Senate; Died in Veterans' Affairs Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on first day of April next succeeding the\ndate after it shall have become law.\n",
